      "title": "Applying Row Operations To a Coefficients Matrix"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "a0046572-b467-5449-a00a-9cb4a2c4539b",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix $C,$ given by\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 8 & 9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the following row operations on $C?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2} \\\\ {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+{R}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's list the required operations:\n\n- The operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2}$ means that we need to add $2$ times the second row to the first row.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{3}$ means that we need to add $1$ times the third row to the first row.\n\nApplying the operations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 8 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\\quad {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & \\sim \\begin{bmatrix}1+(2)(4) & 2+(2)(5) & 3+(2)(6) \\\\ 4 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 8 & 9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\sim \\begin{bmatrix}9 & 12 & 15 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 8 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\\quad {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{3} \\\\  & \\sim \\begin{bmatrix}9+(1)(7) & 12+(1)(8) & 15+(1)(9) \\\\ 4 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 8 & 9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\sim \\begin{bmatrix}16 & 20 & 24 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 8 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
